Addressed the review findings in `3a968a10a`:

- completed graph-cache metadata keys and fixed custom-operator batch broadcasting in fake execution and backward;
- switched the causal-convolution oracle to FP32, removed the unused import, and avoided the lazy-export CodeQL ambiguity;
- made manifest validation reproducible from a clean checkout and ensured CI fetches the pinned source commit;
- reconciled Python, CMake, nanobind, frontend-version, and CuTeDSL requirements with the pinned source; and
- added required SPDX headers, applied the documentation formatters, and regenerated compatibility contracts/snippets.

Validation passes for 47 documentation tests, both manifest/index drift checks, release coverage (277 APIs, 424 candidates, 340 historical topics), the 247-sample catalog, and a clean-clone manifest check without the local `old_docs/` tree.

